5.1 The agreement entered into by the AD with the third party shall in no manner dilute or absolve the AD of its obligations under any statutory or regulatory provision, and the AD shall be fully responsible and liable for all acts and omissions of the third party.
5.2 The agreement of AD with the third party shall explicitly specify the following -
The rights, obligations, and responsibilities of both parties in the transaction flow, including scope of services;
Data handling and confidentiality;
Data privacy;
Dispute resolution mechanisms;
Audit / Information sharing rights (to seek complete details of the transaction and process followed with the checks and balances).
Compliance with applicable laws;
Quoting of exchange rate to the remitter as quoted by AD;
Scope of engagement;
Permitted activities;
Risk mitigation frameworks (including operational resilience and concentration risk management);
Refund policy;
Internal controls for compliance with FEMA, 1999.
5.3 The third party shall have a comprehensive Privacy Policy compliant with applicable laws, associated regulation and RBI guidelines, which shall be made available publicly and accessible easily.

