88. A liquidity facility is provided to help smoothen the timing differences faced by the SPE between the receipt of cash flows from the underlying assets and the payments to be made to investors. A liquidity facility should meet all of the following conditions to guard against the possibility of the facility functioning as a form of credit enhancement and/ or credit support:
(1) All conditions specified in Paragraphs 79 and 80.
(2) The documentation for the facility must clearly define the circumstances under which the facility may or may not be drawn on.
