(ii) Review of high yielding advances sanctioned by the RCB;
(iii) Review of progress in implementation of Govt. sponsored programmes;
(iv) A comprehensive report on the recoveries effected under NPA accounts. The report shall cover requisite details on the deficiencies observed, systemic controls required for avoidance of incidence of NPAs, etc. During the review, the Board shall also look at loan policy caveats on exposure thresholds, borrower-wise/ industry-wise, etc. and other credit risk management initiatives on ongoing basis.
