A. Placement / acceptance of Deposits

127. As per paragraph 120 and 121 above, a UCB fulfilling the following criteria shall have the option to accept deposits from other UCBs:
(1) Applicable minimum CRAR plus 1 per cent;
(2) Gross Non Performing Assets (NPAs) of less than 7 per cent and Net NPAs of not more than 3 per cent;
(3) Net profit for at least three out of the preceding four years subject to it not having incurred a net loss in the immediately preceding year;
(4) No default in the maintenance of CRR / SLR during the preceding financial year;
(5) Sound internal control system with at least two professional directors on the Board; and
(6) Core Banking Solution (CBS) fully implemented.

128. A UCB which has accepted deposits from other UCBs but subsequently fail to meet the criteria provided in paragraph 127 above shall phase out the deposits as under:
(1) 10 per cent of deposits by March 31st of the financial year in which the UCB became ineligible to accept such deposits, and 40 per cent, 70 per cent, and 100 per cent by the end of the following financial years;
(2) During the phase-out period, such a UCB shall not accept further deposits from other UCBs and shall neither open new deposit accounts of any UCB. The renewal of existing deposits is allowed subject to compliance with the phase out plan mentioned above; and
(3) In case the concerned UCB again attains the criteria prescribed in paragraph 127, it shall be eligible to accept deposits from other UCBs and shall not be required to implement the phase out plan;
